# A request that does not fit the model's context window, even after
# kiln tries to compact once (internal/harness/compaction.go's fitRequest
# -> ContextOverflowError): the model's own first reply is big enough on
# its own that the very next turn's request cannot be made to fit, so the
# turn ends with ContextOverflowError's plain-words message instead of a
# panic or a provider-shaped error.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-context-overflow.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE /model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Select model/ 20
KEY down
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Now on faux\/faux-2 · small tier/ 20
TYPE give me all the detail at once
KEY enter
# The ~150k-char reply streams as ~19k faux chunks; a CI runner needs
# well over 90s for it (finding stream-render-cost-grows-with-reply).
WAITFOR /›\s+describe a task/ 300
SHOT huge-reply-landed
TYPE anything else
KEY enter
WAITFOR /does not fit faux\/faux-2's 32\.8k-token window,\s+even after compacting it/ 20
SHOT overflow-error
EXPECT /does not fit faux\/faux-2's 32\.8k-token window,\s+even after compacting it/
EXPECT /\/clear to start over, or \/model to a model with a larger window/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
